# Kidney food reference (Draft of what foods to and to not eat)

Purpose: this is the list the tr4CKD app checks each food against. It summarizes general guidance from the sources below, but as an overall summary rather than direct referencing--check liscensing rules and contuct. THIS IS NOT A SUBSTITUTION TO A DIETITION'S LIST. **Where his dietitian's list differs, the dietitian's list wins.**

Status: DRAFT. Not yet reviewed by a dietitian or doctor. Each rule links to the source it came from.

---

## How the ratings work

| Rating | Meaning | Examples (from the sources below) |
|---|---|---|
| Green | Generally fine in a normal portion | Apples, berries, grapes, pineapple, cauliflower, cabbage, green beans, peppers, onions, white rice, white bread, pasta, unsalted popcorn, unsalted crackers, herbs and spices, olive oil |
| Yellow | Okay in small portions or occasionally | Chicken, turkey, fish, eggs, beans and lentils, carrots, whole-grain bread, low-fat milk or 1 oz cheese a day, plant milks (check labels) |
| Orange | High in one limited nutrient; eat little or swap | Bananas, oranges, melons, potatoes, tomatoes, spinach, avocado, winter squash, raisins, prunes, nuts, seeds, oatmeal, bran cereal, brown or wild rice |
| Red | High in several limited nutrients, or on the avoid list | Processed or cured meats (bacon, ham, sausage, salami, deli meats), fried and fast food, canned or salted foods, salt substitutes with potassium chloride, coconut products, dark colas, foods with "phos" in the ingredients, organ meats |

